Z||000008||firstfiero||08-19-2001||10:27 AM||||      I guess I'm an old fogie...30...but when I was a kid wrestling was so much more fun. The wwf was more of a show but still good. I was a big hulk hogan fan of course. The NWA...befor turner bought it that's what it was called...was more about wrestling and I liked the 4 horseman. In case you don't who that was..Rick flair,arn anderson,Tully blanchard and ole anderson. The uwf was great more blood then I've ever seen befor. The good old wccw with the Von-erichs. And last but not least the Awa. anyway I try to watch it now and their really isn't any wrestling anymore. It's punching and kicking with no real moves. I remember the first time I saw the Great Kubuki do his back flip off the top rope...now that was wrestling. But I'm obviously in the minority.<P>------------------<BR><BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/firstfiero.gif"> ||||reg||1
